        "document_id": "3482",
        "explanation": "Senator Mikulski states, 'I will continue to fight to provide the federal support they need,' and highlights her role on the Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee, explicitly tying her efforts to the funding announcement for firefighters."
      },
      {
        "document_id": "4585",
        "explanation": "Senator Schumer states, 'I was among the first senators who recognized the need for the federal government to establish a funding program,' explicitly claiming credit for his role in advocating for and securing federal fire grants."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator merely discusses, criticizes, or supports an issue, policy, or outcome without explicitly linking it to their own actions or efforts. Statements that are purely informational, expressive of opinion, or focused on others' actions do not qualify as credit-claiming.",
